    "body": "## Objective\n\nSpecify plants, suppliers and arcs with source and flow quantities. On dated purchase and shipment snapshots, compare landed cost against fixed sourcing proportions subject to lead time, capacity and material conservation. Record units, solver capabilities, input rights, integration fields, uncertainty and rejection thresholds before an experiment.\n\n## Scope\n\n- IND02-01 · plants, suppliers and arcs\n\n- IND02-02 · source and flow quantities\n\n- IND02-03 · lead time, capacity and material conservation\n\n- IND02-04 · landed cost\n\n- IND02-05 · dated purchase and shipment snapshots\n\n- IND02-06 · fixed sourcing proportions\n\n## Boundaries and failure behavior\n\nStudy only. Record dataset licensing, unobserved rules and validation risk before any commercial implementation.\n\n## Engineering references\n\nDirective §19 · IND02 · parent #87 (P01). Target module: `docs/sectors`. Architecture: `docs/design/architecture.md`. Diagram/reference: `docs/design/operating-modes.md`. See `planning/requirements.json` for contracts, field readiness and evidence. Implement only after the relevant design/field contracts are reviewed.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n#53 (V06)\n\n## Consumers\n\nRelease review and end users.\n\n## Acceptance and required tests\n\nSpecify plants, suppliers and arcs with source and flow quantities. On dated purchase and shipment snapshots, compare landed cost against fixed sourcing proportions subject to lead time, capacity and material conservation. Record units, solver capabilities, input rights, integration fields, uncertainty and rejection thresholds before an experiment. Study only. Record dataset licensing, unobserved rules and validation risk before any commercial implementation.\n\n## Verification and definition of done\n\nRun `dotnet run --project tools/Traceability` for planning integrity. Attach feature-specific tests, commands, observed pass/fail output and applicable OS/fixture revisions to the implementation PR. Review downstream consumers, field compatibility and recovery behavior. A green planning check establishes structural validity only. Merge under repository policy before closing.\n\n## Planning\n\nP2 · Multi-Sector · research · medium risk.\n\nScope key: IND02",
